# Agent runtime

## 1. Local first
- Prefer Cherry: local Cursor, Cursor CLI, or Pixel driving Cherry — those already have the repo, Godot, and godot-mcp.
- Cursor cloud agents are OK when Pixel / Grok Bot orchestrates them, or when:
  - Cherry is off or asleep and the job can't wait, or
  - Nathan asks for a cloud agent by name, or
  - more than about 3 big jobs must run in parallel.
- Cloud ships still cannot F5 or godot-mcp. Every visual / cabin / UI ship from cloud must leave a `playtest/repot/inbox/` request so local Cursor can verify (see §11 and `playtest-repot.mdc`).

## 2. Work in the playtest folder
- Default: all work happens in `C:\Users\Natha\Documents\boss-rush` (the primary worktree), so Nathan can press F5 and test right away.
- Nathan uploads feedback in batches and tests them in place.
- A worktree under `C:\Users\Natha\Documents\boss-rush-wt\<branch>` is a fallback only. Use one when:
  - the job would overwrite or collide with Nathan's uncommitted edits, or
  - it runs while he's mid-playtest on a different branch.
- Delete fallback worktrees once their PR is merged or closed.
- Never discard or overwrite Nathan's uncommitted changes.

## 3. GitHub is the source of truth
- Every job is committed and pushed.
- Bigger jobs: their own branch and a PR, labeled `ready-to-test` with the `### 🎨 Ready to test from Pixel` note (see `pixel-handoff.mdc`).
- Small jobs: straight to `main` (see `playtest-approve.mdc`).
- Never copy files between folders by hand.

## 4. One job per area at a time
- If two jobs would edit the same files or systems (e.g. both touch the wheel), the second waits.

## 5. Pick the model to fit the job
- Cheaper model for mechanical work: wiring in art, recolors, renames, cleanups.
- Stronger model only for real design or tricky code.

## 6. Go easy on Cherry while Nathan plays
- Run heavy headless Godot jobs (import, screenshot QA) at low priority.
- Anything that needs the editor window waits until he isn't playing.
- Never kill Godot processes you didn't start.

## 7. The cloud project stays paused
- The old Cursor cloud handoff project (Official, `bc-96e5315d`) stays parked unless Nathan revives it.

## 8. Same steps every time = script, not agent
- If the steps never change, they live in a script under `tools/dev/` (see `tools/dev/README.md`). Agents must call the script instead of redoing the steps by hand:
  - `load-pr.ps1 <n|branch>`: "load it". Stashes WIP, checks out the PR branch, re-applies the WIP.
  - `back-to-main.ps1`: "not yet" / switch back. Same stash dance, then `pull --ff-only`.
  - `ready-prs.ps1`: the per-message `ready-to-test` check. Prints nothing when there's nothing.
  - `godot-check.ps1 [path]`: headless import + parse check at low priority. Prints `Godot: N errors`.
  - `clean-import-churn.ps1`: drops `.import` uid/line-ending churn before a commit.
  - `install-hooks.ps1`: turns on the pre-commit guard.
- If a script fails, report its output. Don't hand-roll a workaround.

## 9. Hard limits live in code
- `tools/hooks/pre-commit` blocks:
  - secrets: literal tokens, a non-`${env:...}` credential in `.cursor/mcp.json`;
  - local-only files: `.art-ping.env`, `.art-ping.last`, `.wrangler/`, `build/`;
  - `Tier` / `ATK` / `atk` in player-facing copy.
- Never bypass it with `--no-verify`. If it blocks something you believe is fine, stop and ask Nathan.

## 10. Keep automatic check-ins rare
- No scheduled or recurring agent runs for this game. Nathan starts things.

## 11. Cloud agents must write a repot request
- Whenever a cloud agent (or any agent without godot-mcp) ships a visual / cabin / UI change, it MUST add or update `playtest/repot/inbox/REQ-*.md` in the same PR per `playtest/repot/SCHEMA.md` before claiming done.
- Local Cursor drains inbox via `playtest-repot.mdc`.
- Never mark your own request `done`.
